:::container
:::grid {cols-2 loose}
:::card {bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900 padded-xl}
WORK IN PROGRESS {small bold muted}

## A field guide to better work {serif text-3xl}

One question, a few observations, and a next step. Enough structure to move an idea forward without burying it in a template. {relaxed-lines}

:badge[Draft]{secondary} :badge[Open for feedback]{info}
:::

:::card {padded-xl}
### Start with the essential {large bold}

What should your reader understand, feel, or do after this page?

:::definitions
**The question** {term}
: Give the work a clear purpose.

**The evidence** {term}
: Make room for the details that matter.

**The next step** {term}
: Leave a useful path forward.
:::
:::
:::
:::

---

:::container
## Less friction. More room to think. {text-3xl bold #approach}

Three building blocks for a page that feels considered. {large muted}

:::grid {cols-3 loose}
:::card {padded}
:icon[type]{primary large}

### Let the words lead

Use headings, lists, and emphasis to make the reading order clear. Keep the source as approachable as the finished page.
:::

:::card {padded}
:icon[layout]{primary large}

### Compose with purpose

Combine cards, grids, and callouts when they help a reader compare, explore, or decide. Leave space around the important parts.
:::

:::card {padded}
:icon[download]{primary large}

### Keep the finished work

Export a portable HTML page. Your reader can open it offline, switch themes, and print it without an account.
:::
:::
:::

---

:::container {narrow}
## From a thought to something shared {text-3xl bold #process}

:::steps {numbered connected}
### Write {step completed}
Put the idea into plain language. Keep one main thought per section.

### Shape {step current}
Choose the right components, tune the typography, and check the page at a smaller width.

### Share {step}
Save the source, export the page, and open the exported file to experience it as your reader will.
:::

---

## Make this page your own. {text-3xl bold #start}

Fieldnotes is an example composition made with Taildown. Replace the words, change the palette, or use it as the starting point for an entirely different page. {large relaxed-lines}

[Open the Taildown editor](https://taildown.dev/editor){button primary}

Save a copy of this `.td` file, open it in the editor, and choose **Design settings** from **Command-K** to try a different typographic direction. {small muted}
:::
